# Copy to .env and edit, or just run `./install.sh`. `docker compose` reads
# this automatically.

# --- Postgres -------------------------------------------------------------
# Password for the bundled Postgres container. Change it before first boot;
# it is baked into the database on the very first `up`.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme

# --- Media ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The host directory that holds your media. Must be an ABSOLUTE path. It is
# bind-mounted into the container at the SAME path, so absolute paths already in
# your database keep working after the move to Docker. Point the library
# variables below at subfolders of it.
SAMO_MEDIA_HOST_DIR=/mnt/media

# Library folders (inside the container = same as on the host). Separate
# multiple folders with a colon, e.g. /mnt/media/Music:/mnt/media/More.
SAMO_MUSIC_DIRS=/mnt/media/Music
SAMO_AUDIOBOOK_DIRS=/mnt/media/Audiobooks
SAMO_PODCAST_DIRS=/mnt/media/Podcasts

# --- First-run admin (optional) ------------------------------------------
# Leave both blank to create the admin through the web /setup wizard instead.
SAMO_BOOTSTRAP_USERNAME=
SAMO_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=

# --- Integrations (optional) ---------------------------------------------
SAMO_LASTFM_API_KEY=
SAMO_LASTFM_SHARED_SECRET=
SAMO_ACOUSTID_API_KEY=

# --- outbound egress, for a box behind a VPN kill-switch -------------------
# Routes ONLY the hosts listed below through a CONNECT proxy on a machine whose
# default route is the plain WAN (see the samo-proxy repo), instead of the VPN.
#
# Why: some CDNs refuse commercial VPN exit addresses. Deezer's is the case this
# was built for — api.deezer.com answers normally while cdn-images.dzcdn.net
# returns 403 to every request, so artist photos are found and never downloaded.
#
# Traffic routed this way does NOT go through the VPN, and an artwork URL names
# something in your library. Leave unset (the default) and nothing changes:
# every request keeps the box's normal route. The host list is closed, and the
# Deezer *lookup* deliberately stays on the VPN.
#
# The proxy is preferred, never required. If it is unreachable, refuses the
# token, or is simply not running, samo-server logs it once and falls back to
# the box's ordinary route — which is the VPN, i.e. the MORE private path, so
# there is nothing to weigh. The worst case is that artwork goes back to
# failing the way it did before, not that requests error out. After a failure
# the proxy is skipped for two minutes so a long backfill does not pay its
# dial timeout once per artist.
SAMO_EGRESS_PROXY_URL=
# Optional. Defaults to Deezer's image CDN and nothing else.
SAMO_EGRESS_PROXY_HOSTS=


# --- Behavior (optional; these are the defaults) -------------------------
# SAMO_SCAN_ON_START=false
# SAMO_PODCAST_POLL=true
# SAMO_ADDR=:6969
